<div>
    <p>Checkout entry points: <code>POST /api/orders</code> (cart checkout, guest-allowed via the <code>allow_guest_checkout</code> setting) and <code>POST /api/orders/quick</code> (single-product buy-now). Both go through <code>OrderService</code>, which prices lines via <code>PromotionEngine</code>, reserves stock, and logs promotion/promo-code usage.</p>
    <p>Line items (<code>OrderProduct</code>) and the status timeline (<code>OrderHistory</code>) are managed by the checkout engine, not hand-edited in the admin form.</p>
    <p><code>delivery_method</code>/<code>delivery_type</code>/<code>payment_method</code> are plain strings validated against <code>deliveries.key</code>/<code>delivery_types.key</code>/<code>payment_methods.code</code>.</p>
    <p>Shipment tracking (<code>App\Nexus\Modules\Shipment\*</code>) isn't its own admin module — its one admin action (<code>POST /admin/shipment/{order}/refresh</code>) is registered here since <code>OrderShipment</code> is 1:1 with an order. <code>php artisan shipment:refresh-statuses</code> polls every non-terminal shipment for Nova Poshta (<code>delivery_method</code> key <code>nova-poshta</code>) / Ukrposhta (<code>ukr-poshta</code>) — not scheduled automatically, schedule it if either carrier is enabled. Carrier credentials: <code>config/novaposhta.php</code> (<code>NP_API_KEY</code>), <code>config/ukrposhta.php</code> (<code>UP_STATUS_TRACKING_BEARER</code>).</p>
</div>
